<p>Another thing to consider is the possibility that <code>max_subarray(i -=
 1)</code> is negative. This would mean the max subarray should only consis=
t of -9, as a further negative contribution will only decrease the sum. The=
refore, the formula becomes:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><code>max_subarray(i) =3D max(max_subarray(i - 1) + nums[i], nums[i])</c=
ode></p>
</blockquote>
<p>As we see, this is a <strong>recurrence relation</strong> that takes adv=
antage of an <strong>optimal substructure</strong>, where the max subarray =
at the current index depends on the max subarray at the previous index.</p>
<p>This indicates we can solve this problem using DP. Translating the above=
 recurrence relation to a DP formula gives us:</p>
<blockquote>
<p><code>dp[i] =3D max(dp[i - 1] + nums[i], nums[i])</code></p>
</blockquote>
<p>Now, let=E2=80=99s consider what the base case for this problem is.</p>
